<title>FRANCE: CYCLING-INJURED BOARDMAN RIDES ON.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-INJURED BOARDMAN RIDES ON.</headline>
<dateline>LOUDENVIELLE, France 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Briton Chris Boardman will continue in the Tour de France despite a fall on Monday in which he displaced two vertebrae in his neck.</p>
<p>&quot;If it had been any other race I would be going home. I have stressed the back of my neck and it's difficult to turn my head. Otherwise I don't forsee any problems,&quot; said Boardman, who dropped from third to 72nd overall as a result of his crash in the Pyrenees.</p>
</text>
